Z||000000||daveml66||10-31-2001||12:19 AM||||would a 3.1 from  a  96 monte carlo bolt up to the fiero trans like earlier 3.1s?????||||reg||5
Z||000001||Voytek||11-02-2001||01:08 PM||||No.  The earlier 3.1's are 60 degree engines (a 60 degree V  between the cylinders) and the later ones are 90 degree engines - different animal.<P>You could probably make it work but I think it'd be too much fuss.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Shaun41178||11-02-2001||02:22 PM||||Actually voyetk the 3.1 from a 96 lumina is a 6 degree engine.  Yes it will bolt up to the Fiero tranny and should bolt up to the front mount.  However a new dogbone will have to be fabricated.  Its not that direct of a  swap.  Perhaps Joe Torma will see this as he put a 3400 engine in his Fiero which is kind of the same as the 3100 you are asking about.<P>But to answer your question again the 3100 will bolt up to the tranny||||reg||1
